{"strongs": "H1272", "word": "בָּרַח", "translit": "ba.rach", "root": "ברח", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "go through, flee", "definition": "בָּרַח verb go through, flee (compare German durchgehen (Arabic go away, withdraw, flee ) — Qal Perfect בָּרַח Gen 31:22 + 9 t., בָּֽרְחוּ Job 9:25 , בָּרָ֑חוּ Isa 22:3 Imperfect יִבְרַח Job 20:24 , יִבְרָ֑ח Job 27:22 ; Neh 6:11 , וַיִּבְרַח Gen 31:21 + 13 t.; 3 feminine singular וַתִּבְרַח Gen 16:6 , אֶבְרָ֑ח Ps 139:7 , יִבְרְחוּ Jer 52:7 , וַיִּבְרְחוּ 2Sam 4:3 + 4 t., נִבְרָחָ֑ה 2Sam 15:14 Imperative בְּרַח Gen 27:43 + 3 t., בִּרְחוּ Isa 48:20 Infinitive absolute בָּרוֺחַ Job 27:22 construct בְּרֹחַ 1Sam 23:6 + 3 t., בִּרוֺחַ Jonah 1:3 suffix בָּרְחִי 1Kgs 2:7 , בָּרְחֲךָ Gen 31:5 , בָּרְחוֺ Gen 35:7 + 2 t.; — 1. go or pass though , of bar, וַיַּעַשׂ אֶתהַֿבְּרִיחַלִ֗֗֗בְרֹחַ Exod 36:33 ( P ). 2. flee Gen 31:20 ; Gen 21:21 ; Gen 31:22 ( E ) Exod 14:5 ( J ) Judg 9:21 ; 1Sam 19:12 ; 1Sam 19:18 ; 1Sam 22:17 ; 2Sam 13:34 ; 2Sam 13:37 ; 2Sam 13:38 (strike out Dr compare We ) 2Sam 15:14 ; Isa 22:3 ; Jer 4:29 ; Jer 26:21 ; Jer 39:4 ; Jer 52:7 ; Neh 6:11 figurative of days fleeing away Job 9:25 of man, like a shadow Job 14:2 with מִן flee from a place 1Sam 20:1 ; 2Sam 19:10 9 + מֵעַל person) Isa 48:20 , a weapon Job 20:24 a person, with מֵאֵת 1Kgs 11:23 , usually with מִפְּנֵי Gen 16:6 ; Gen 16:8 ; Gen 31:27 ; Gen 35:1 ; Gen 35:7 ; Exod 2:15 (all J E ) Judg 11:3 ; 2Sam 21:11 ; 1Kgs 2:7 ; 1Kgs 12:2 = 2Chr 10:2 ; Ps 3:1 ; Ps 57:1 (titles) Ps 139:7 ; Jonah 1:10 ׳ מִיַּד י figurative Job 27:22 flee to , with accusative place 1Sam 27:4 ; 1Kgs 11:40 ; Hos 12:13 with place & לְ Neh 13:10 with place & ָ ה locative Jonah 1:3 ; Jonah 4:2 ; 2Sam 4:3 with place & אֶלֿ Num 24:11 ; Amos 7:12 with אֶלֿ & person 1Sam 23:6 ; Gen 27:43 ( J ) 1Kgs 2:39 ; 1Kgs 11:40 אַחֲרֵי & person 1Sam 22:20 flee , followed by infinitive 1Kgs 11:17 ; Dan 10:7 . 3. flee = hasten, come quickly Song 8:14 . Hiph`il Perfect הִבְרִיחוּ 1Chr 8:13 Imperfect יַבְרִ